From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 10:36:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/i915/dp: a refused request of the tunnel through a
 converter is said once, not as an error

intel_dp_pcon_dv_compute_config() (linux-9977) gives the reasons of a
refusal to DVBRIDGE_REFUSED, whose report says them in the kernel log
(drm_dvbridge_refused_report(): at info level and rate limited, as for
every refusal of the tunnel on HDMI), and then said the same detail again
with drm_err(). A request that the policy refuses is no fault of the
driver: it was in the log twice, once among the errors of the system,
where a reading of the errors takes it for one. The second line is gone;
the warning when a request goes through a converter that nobody has seen
carry the tunnel stays.

Host test: intel_dp_pcon_dv_compute_config() has no drm_err() and still
gives a refusal to DVBRIDGE_REFUSED; it fails without this change. W=1 on
i915 and xe: no warning.
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_dp.c | 5 +----
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_dp.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_dp.c
index 560edf438..5ed1dad5c 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_dp.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_dp.c
@@ -3741,11 +3741,8 @@ static int intel_dp_pcon_dv_compute_config(struct intel_dp *intel_dp,
 			  link.colorspace, link.width, link.height, link.rounded_refresh,
 			  link.progressive ? "" : ", not progressive 2D", link.cloned ? ", cloned" : "",
 			  crtc_state->dsc.compression_enable ? ", DSC" : "");
+		/* (the kernel log says it with DVBRIDGE_REFUSED, as for native HDMI) */
 		intel_dp_pcon_dv_refused(connector, bits, detail);
-		if (__ratelimit(&limit))
-			drm_err(display->drm,
-				"[CONNECTOR:%d:%s] DVBRIDGE: the tunnel through the DisplayPort to HDMI converter was refused: %s\n",
-				connector->base.base.id, connector->base.name, detail);
 		return ret ?: -EINVAL;
 	}
 
